==========================================================
USE EXISTING PURCHASE HISTORY AS REFERENCE DATA
===============================================

This is important.

Do not ask Ollama to determine Common Names in isolation if ShopGraph already
contains examples that can guide normalization.

Build useful reference context from existing Purchase History rows whose Common
Name is already populated.

For example, if Purchase History contains:

```
Product:
    DOVE MEN+CARE BODY WASH CLEAN COMFORT

Common Name:
    Body Wash
```

then that existing mapping is useful evidence when Ollama encounters another
similar Dove body wash product.

Prefer consistency with ShopGraph's existing Common Name vocabulary over
inventing new terminology.

Where practical, provide Ollama with relevant existing:

```
Product -> Common Name
```

examples.

Do not dump the entire Purchase History into every request if unnecessary.

Select relevant examples or construct a compact reference vocabulary.

==========================================================
DETERMINISTIC MATCH BEFORE AI
=============================

Before calling Ollama, attempt safe deterministic reuse of existing mappings.

For example, if the exact normalized Product value has previously appeared in
Purchase History with one consistent Common Name:

```
Product:
    BANANAS
```

existing mapping:

```
BANANAS -> Bananas
```

then ShopGraph may safely reuse:

```
Bananas
```

without asking Ollama.

Only do this when the existing mapping is unambiguous.

If the same Product has conflicting historical Common Names, do NOT guess.

Send that row to Ollama with the conflicting examples as context if useful.

This provides the preferred order:

```
1. Exact reliable existing ShopGraph mapping
2. Ollama inference using ShopGraph context
3. Leave unresolved if confidence/validation is insufficient
```

Never silently invent a value merely to make validation pass.

