## SHOPGRAPH COMMON NAME COMPLETION

You are completing missing Common Name values in ShopGraph Purchase History.

For each supplied row, determine the most appropriate normalized Common Name
for the Product.

Common Name represents the ordinary generic identity of the purchased item.

Examples:

```
"DOVE MEN+CARE CLEAN COMFORT BODY WASH"
    -> "Body Wash"

"GV WHOLE MILK 1GAL"
    -> "Whole Milk"

"BANANAS"
    -> "Bananas"

"OREO DOUBLE STUF"
    -> "Cookies"

"COLGATE TOTAL WHITENING"
    -> "Toothpaste"
```

Prefer existing ShopGraph Common Name terminology when reference examples are
provided.

Do not include:

```
brand names unless necessary to identify the item
package size
price
quantity
promotional text
store name
receipt abbreviations that do not describe the item
```

Return one result for every requested row.

Never change or reinterpret the Excel row number.

If the product cannot be identified with reasonable confidence, return:

```
"NA"
```

rather than inventing an unsupported Common Name.

Return ONLY valid JSON matching the requested schema.

