==========================================================
STRUCTURED OLLAMA RESPONSE
==========================

Do not parse conversational prose.

Require strict structured JSON.

Preferred schema:

```
{
  "rows": [
    {
      "excel_row": 267,
      "common_name": "Body Wash"
    },
    {
      "excel_row": 268,
      "common_name": "Whole Milk"
    }
  ]
}
```

Every requested Excel row must appear exactly once.

No unexpected Excel rows may appear.

==========================================================
STRICT RESPONSE VALIDATION
==========================

Before changing the workbook, validate the entire Ollama response.

Check:

1. Response is valid JSON.
2. Top-level structure is correct.
3. `rows` exists and is a list.
4. Every requested row appears exactly once.
5. No unrequested row appears.
6. No duplicate Excel row numbers exist.
7. `common_name` is a string.
8. Common Name is normalized/trimmed.
9. Empty strings are rejected.
10. The target workbook row still has blank/NA Common Name before writing.
11. The row number maps to the same source Product that was sent to Ollama.

That last check is important.

Do not allow an AI response to accidentally update the wrong Excel row.

==========================================================
HANDLING OLLAMA "NA"
====================

Ollama is allowed to return:

```
NA
```

when there is insufficient evidence.

Do NOT convert an uncertain answer into a fabricated Common Name merely to
satisfy Category Manager validation.

If some rows remain unresolved, report them clearly:

```
[WARNING] Common Name completion was incomplete.

Updated rows: 5
Unresolved rows: 1

Remaining blank/NA Common Name rows:
- Row 271: Product = "XYZ ABC 14OZ"

Category Manager Completion will continue to reject Purchase History
until these rows are resolved.
```

This preserves data quality.

